# Core architecture

## Data flow

Browser (`components/`) → `fetch /api/*` → Route Handlers (`app/api/`) → `lib/*` → HydraDB / OpenAI.

## Server-only secrets

API keys and external clients live only in `lib/*` (and Route Handlers that call `lib/*`). Never read `process.env` for secrets in client components.

## MVP constraints (do not add unless explicitly requested)

- No authentication
- No in-repo database (HydraDB is the memory store)
- No background jobs, Redis, or file uploads
- No global state libraries (Redux, Zustand, React Query)
- Single sub-tenant: `mvp_user` in `lib/hydradb.ts`

## Next.js 16

This project uses Next.js 16 with breaking API changes. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using App Router features. Heed deprecation notices.

## Where code belongs

| Concern | Location |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP validation + response | `app/api/*/route.ts` |
| Business logic, SDK calls | `lib/*.ts` |
| Zod schemas | `lib/validation.ts` |
| Shared types | `lib/types.ts` |
| UI | `components/` (feature) or `components/ui/` (shadcn primitives) |
